=92 repost detection =E2=86=92
employer hiring velocity =E2=86=92 apprenticeship supply-response index.

Joins: UKGraph ONS Textkernel jobs, Companies House, DfE apprenticeship
starts/achievements, Nomis labour supply, SIC/SOC, local geography.

Buyer hypothesis: workforce planners, training providers, recruiters, FE
colleges, local authorities, investors/consultancies studying
skilled-labour constraints. Buyer evidence is currently INFERRED rather
than directly priced, so capped.

Time moat: HIGH. Historic aggregate apprenticeship statistics exist, but
exact advert-level state, reposts, location changes and duration are not
obviously offered as a complete public point-in-time archive.

First collector: poll current adverts at least daily; preserve raw response
hash plus normalized advert state. Test whether IDs persist across
edits/reposts.

Falsifier: discovery of a complete, cheap, advert-level historical archive
including revisions and expiry state.
