4) DEFRA Digital Waste Tracking =E2=80=94 WATCH, do not misclassify

CONFIRMED: public beta began 28 April 2026; mandatory receipt reporting
begins 1 October 2026 in England/Wales and January 2027 in Scotland/NI.
Phase 2 for collectors begins private beta in autumn 2026. DEFRA says the
industry includes ~12,000 waste-site operators, ~150,000 exemption holders
and ~300,000 carriers/brokers/dealers. Receipt API v1.1 was issued 10 April
2026 and uses seven REST endpoints. Every incoming movement eventually
receives a tracking ID.

Critical counterevidence: current Receipt API is authenticated submission
infrastructure, not an open national read API. We cannot assume movement
records are publicly collectable. This blocks a national raw-data forest
today.

Why monitor: if aggregate/open read access appears, or if we operate
software for consenting sites, the dataset is extraordinarily early and
structurally new. DEFRA=E2=80=99s own impact assessment says existing waste=
 data is
incomplete, inconsistent and fragmented; the new system is intended to
centralize movement tracking.

