   irreversible feed.

Reconstruction tests / exclusions

REJECT raw EA water-quality API as a new-feed moat: the 2025/26 API changed
access mechanics, but available commentary indicates it serves
substantially the same historical archive; API novelty does not equal data
novelty.

REJECT raw NESO 2026 FES tables as time moat: current CKAN API makes them
machine-readable, but annual scenario vintages are already explicitly
published and preserved.

REJECT Binance/KuCoin WebSocket architecture changes: new
endpoints/transport structure do not create a novel underlying dataset;
deep crypto market-history vendors already exist.

REJECT generic Find a Tender collection as a new-feed opportunity: robust
